16#,#16-ENG Major#,#Engineering (Aeronautics and Astronautics)#,#Bachelor of Science in Engineering as Recommended by the Department of Aeronautics and Astronautics

Course 16-ENG is an engineering degree program designed to offer flexibility within the context of aerospace engineering and is a complement to our Course 16 aerospace engineering degree program. The 16-ENG degree is accredited by the Engineering Accreditation Commission of ABET.

concentration_electives

%% Concentration electives - must choose 72 units total with at least 42 units of engineering topics and 12 units of mathematics or science topics
%% Course 16 electives are listed first (aerospace engineering specific)
%% Additional engineering courses from other departments are included for the 42 unit engineering requirement
%% Math and science courses are included for the 12 unit math/science requirement

concentration_electives, "Concentration" := aero_core_electives, aero_advanced_electives, other_engineering_electives, math_science_electives{>=72u}

%% Core AeroAstro electives (most suitable for concentration themes)
